WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.960
- One, two, three, go!

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.960
Hi! Welcome to a new episode of Project Kamp!

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.120
In this video, you will see us harvesting some potatoes
with our very direct neighbors.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.120
Because, this is our land...

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.880
And, this is Antonio's and Fernanda's land.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.571
They asked us for some help.

00:00:16.571 --> 00:00:20.400
Afterwards, we will also harvest our veggie box.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.400
And, we will explain to you a bit more on why we do that.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.760
And, this year, we have been visited
by a lot of wild animals.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.440
And, at the end, you will see a very, very, very cute visit,
that we had from some friends.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.960
I hope you enjoy it!

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.520
- So, what is the plan for now, guys?

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:47.400
We are going to harvest some potatoes,
to help out Fernanda and Antonio, our closest neighbors.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:49.920
Ready?

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.920
- Ready!

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:43.320
Okay, so, harvesting potatoes on Fernanda's
and Antonio's field goes like this:

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.040
You choose either to dig, or to pick.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.480
If you choose to dig...

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.560
You take the hoe, hit the soil
exactly at the edge of the water ditch...

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.160
Make it loose, and search for the little tasty gems.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Then, you throw them behind you, and repeat.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.520
You need to dig hard enough to go deep.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.520
But, at the same time, gentle and precise.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.120
Otherwise, you will damage or cut the potatoes in half...

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.409
Which will be then followed by a less happy Antonio/Fernanda...

00:02:15.409 --> 00:02:18.880
Who then gives you a private lesson on how to work properly.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.417
If you choose to pick, it's easier.

00:02:22.417 --> 00:02:28.400
You just throw the fresh, harvested potatoes in the bucket,
 and for damaged and two small ones in another.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.920
Nevertheless, you're going to be exhausted anyway,
since it's a huge field, it's super hot...

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.600
The potatoes don't come out of the soil by themselves!

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.680
- Did you understand what he said?

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.922
Just the good potatoes!

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.787
The next step is simple!

00:04:06.787 --> 00:04:11.520
Hop on Antonio's tractor, and take a ride to the tiny house,
where they store the potatoes.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.080
Don't forget to enjoy the lovely Portuguese countryside!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.600
The right is short,
but be careful to not fall off the tractor.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:23.920
Since the road is quite bumpy,
and you are sitting on the side of a giant shovel...

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:30.400
Then, hop up, empty the buckets,
and start again from the beginning.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:51.216
If you made it to this point, congratulations!

00:06:51.216 --> 00:06:53.280
You have passed the neighborly potato test!

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:57.240
You can see yourself now
as a true Portuguese neighbor.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.120
And, you will be rewarded soon,
with a typical Portuguese boucher!

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:09.680
A delicious snack, which in our case is 
crispy sardines, local cheese, bread...

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:13.000
Fried, and sweet flour balls...

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.000
And, three bottles of tasty homemade wine.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.115
- Fernanda is asking if you're making a video!

00:07:46.115 --> 00:07:46.658
Yes!

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:09.000
So, today we are here at Nunu and Sarah's place.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:12.880
They are friends and they are also farmers.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:17.080
They are usually the ones,
that bring a veggie box to us.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:19.160
Which we showed in a video last season!

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.567
You might remember them!

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.320
Today, it's different.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.320
Today, we come here to their place
to harvest our box.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.120
This is why we want to explain
slightly why we are doing this.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:34.040
So, Sarah and Nuno are part of a network of farmers,
which is called CSA.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:37.280
That stands for 'Community Supported Agriculture'.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:44.120
And, that stands for also creating a link,
between farmers and consumers.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:49.160
So, that it's like a shared responsibility
between risks and rewards.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.520
Because, being a small farmer, it involves a lot of risks.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:58.903
In the sense of that they are dependent on a lot of variables, 
that are beyond their hands...

00:08:58.903 --> 00:09:04.894
Such as whether, as water supply, 
as actually health and strength in their body.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:09.610
This is actually the case on why we are here, 
because Nuno got sick...

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:15.360
It means that Sarah is not able 
to take care of the garden and harvest.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.360
Also, to make the boxes and distribute it all by herself.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:23.080
So, we as consumers come here,
and harvest the box ourselves.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:28.720
- I've tried to seed some carrots on the side!

00:09:30.416 --> 00:09:33.496
Come on through!

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.680
- Zucchini?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.515
Yeah! Come on down here!

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.400
Yellow courgettes!

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.840
Either you twist it, or you can use a knife.

00:09:51.949 --> 00:09:54.326
Courgettes are surprisingly spiky!

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.320
You have to take a yellow one back as well!

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:04.920
Oh, my God!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.560
These are really nice!

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:28.580
I harvested this line...

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.880
- Okay, so, what's going to happen now?

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:40.600
So, now part of the mission is to harvest 
some of the delicious, super big strawberries.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:42.440
Look at this guy over here!

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:46.024
- That's pretty perfect!

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.000
So, maybe it would be easier for you guys,
to understand what actually CSA means.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:24.198
Sarah will answer a few questions.

00:11:24.198 --> 00:11:29.040
Maybe you could say why you chose to become part of CSA?

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:41.587
So, yeah, Community Supported Agriculture is interesting
for both us and the clients.

00:11:41.587 --> 00:11:51.184
From our point of view, and from any farmer that's doing CSA,
 it's interesting, because you have a certain security.

00:11:51.184 --> 00:11:55.880
It's subscription-based, so it's easier to plan your farm.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:12:03.680
You have that sort of base income that you can
 sort of rely on, and at least near to long term.

00:12:05.873 --> 00:12:13.400
It also means that with the box kind of products,
 we can diversify in our farm.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:18.661
Which is not only good for the environment, 
but it also means that makes us more resilient.

00:12:18.661 --> 00:12:23.520
Things like crop failures or strange weather,
which is happening more and more.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:30.000
You know, one product might suffer,
but then we still have other stuff, that we can put in the boxes.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:39.772
For the communities of the people who buy the boxes,
 it's interesting, because it's more local.

00:12:39.772 --> 00:12:41.680
So, your food will be fresher by a ton.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:47.040
And, actually, the quality of the food is often better.

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:50.040
Not just because of the farming techniques, but...

00:12:50.961 --> 00:12:55.400
Nowadays, products can be harvested before they're ready.

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.400
So that they travel better!

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:04.480
That sort of has a negative effect,
on the nutrients and vitamins that you find in your food.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:07.120
So, it's healthy for you too!

00:13:07.885 --> 00:13:10.709
And, it reduces food mass!

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.680
Does that answer your question?

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:18.440
- You answered like three questions I had!

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:19.847
Okay, perfect!

00:13:19.847 --> 00:13:22.080
- It's benificial for you!

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.160
You had it prepared!

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:31.673
Maybe one more question is this:
''Are there any downsides of being part of this CSA?''

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:39.280
Sometimes, it can be a little bit challenging,
 to get the planning right.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:47.200
So, quantities, so, you know, you got to have enough 
diversity in the food box, but also enough of quantities.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.360
That makes sense.

00:13:50.172 --> 00:13:54.040
That, with time, is getting better a lot,
because it was more difficult in the first year.

00:13:55.923 --> 00:13:59.047
So, yeah, practice makes perfect!

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:01.796
- Cool, Sarah! Thank you!

00:14:01.796 --> 00:14:05.160
That's it for the interview,
 and I think we can continue with the harvest!

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.517
If you're happy, I am happy!

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:49.000
So, yesterday, we harvested really beautiful veggies,
for an incredible diverse basket.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.240
Which I wanted to show you now!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.880
There are a few things missing, like the strawberries.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.605
They were too delicious to wait for today.

00:14:57.892 --> 00:15:05.101
But, I just want you to see this richness
 in colors, nutrients and flavors!

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:11.120
We got potatoes, we got fresh garlic...

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:18.603
We got a lot of aromatics, edible flowers, cabbage, kohlrabi...

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:23.160
Zucchini in different colors!

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.280
Some basil...

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.680
Yeah, summer is coming

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.680
And, with summer, a lot of diversity is coming.

00:15:31.997 --> 00:15:35.997
Within the scheme of CSA, as we explained a little bit...

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:40.920
When something is missing, they replace it with something else.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.480
In this case: yesterday, we didn't get lettuce.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:49.040
So, we got extra beans, which sounds like a very cool deal.

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:54.000
We get this box once a week, which is a big luxury for us!

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.910
And, yeah, this is it!

00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:01.280
For now, I just take the box back,
so that Agnes can do her magic.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:15.120
They fell into the water!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.600
- Really?

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:19.160
They could be, because they followed Otis!

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:29.760
Last week, we got visited by some new cute neighbors.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:36.800
It seems they live close by in the mountains, because they just followed 
Otis and Debbie, where they worked on the yoga deck.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:42.560
The mom and dad were also there, 
but they got scared by Otis and ran away!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.560
For some reason, the puppies didn't.

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:51.320
We played a bit with them and then brought them back to the mountains,
 where the parents were able to find them.

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:54.160
It worked fine with the two of them.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:59.720
We also saw them with the mother, 
but the little fellow with the white paws came back to us a few times.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:04.280
We called him Brutus first, then Johnny, then Fling-Flong.

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:07.240
He really seems to like us!

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:12.240
But yeah, we still tried to bring him back to his mother,
so we said goodbye to him.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.880
Let's see if it was for the last time!

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:20.920
That's it for this video!

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:22.800
I hope you guys enjoyed this episode!

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:27.080
If you like what we do in Project Kamp,
 you can also support us on Patreon!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:30.320
You will actually see our videos one week ahead.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:33.320
You can also vote for our thumbnail!

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.560
Next week, we will do a review on our electric chainsaw.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:42.680
For today, we have so many potatoes and I need to cut some...

